Source
------

Original model: https://tfhub.dev/google/yamnet/1
Upstream project: https://github.com/tensorflow/models
                  (research/audioset/yamnet)

Modifications
-------------

This file is NOT the upstream artifact. It is the upstream TensorFlow SavedModel
converted to ONNX, with the graph narrowed to the score head only:

  * Exported via tf2onnx (opset 17) from the official TF-Hub SavedModel.
  * The graph exposes ONE input — a 1-D float32 waveform of arbitrary length,
    mono 16 kHz, range [-1, 1] — and ONE output, `scores [frames, 521]`.
  * YAMNet's other two outputs (the 1024-dim embeddings and the log-mel
    spectrogram) are dropped; only the AudioSet class scores are exported.
  * Model weights are unchanged. The conversion was validated against the
    original TensorFlow model on identical inputs: maximum score difference
    1.2e-06, 100% top-class agreement.

The AudioSet class ordering is the upstream 521-class ordering; no relabelling
or fine-tuning has been applied.
